<title>BELGIUM: UNION MINIERE IN ZAIRE COBALT DEAL - PAPER.</title>
<headline>UNION MINIERE IN ZAIRE COBALT DEAL - PAPER.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian metals group Union Miniere and South African mining firm Anglo American will work on a joint cobalt and copper project in Zaire's Shaba province, the Financieel Economische Tijd newspaper said on Saturday.</p>
<p>Zaire's Gecamines will also be involved in the project which the paper said would involve an investment of between six and nine billion francs.</p>
<p>The new business will take over the business and premises of purifier KZC, Concentrateur Kolwezi, and over 10-years produce 80,000 tonnes of pure copper and 6,000 tonnes of pure cobalt.</p>
<p>A Union Miniere spokesman told the paper the project was in the works but that no formal accord yet existed between Gecamines and Anglo American.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
